    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d860">

                <pb facs="0987" n="793" xml:id="pg793"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Pauley Piles</note>
                <head>No. 860<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States Delegation Working
                        Paper</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d860-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-sibling-dates" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1945-07-20T23:59:59+03:00"
                            notBefore="1945-07-19T00:00:00+03:00">Undated</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Proposed Text</hi></p>
                <p>17. One of the primary purposes of occupation is to obtain reparation for the
                    damage and injury caused Allied countries by German aggression. To accomplish
                    this purpose some importation of raw materials and other items will be
                    necessary. The Control Council shall formulate as soon as possible a program of
                    minimum required imports for Germany as a whole. Such a program shall include
                    provision for equitable inter-zonal distribution of supplies available within
                    Germany, so as to minimize the net deficit for, and imports into, Germany as a
                    whole. Responsibility for the procurement and financing of approved imports for
                    Germany as a whole shall be shared on a basis to be negotiated in the Control
                        Council.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d860-f2"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d860-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d860-f1-content">
                <p>Authorship not indicated.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d860-f2" n="2" xml:id="d860-f2-content">
                <p>The following final sentence has been stricken from the draft: “Reimbursement for
                    all net advances made for approved imports into Germany shall be a first charge
                    against the proceeds of any exports from Germany of current production and
                    stocks of goods.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
